---
import i18next, { t, changeLanguage } from "i18next";
import { localizePath, localizeUrl } from "astro-i18next";
import { Trans } from "astro-i18next/components";
import Layout from "../layouts/BlogPost.astro";

changeLanguage("en");
---

<Layout
	title={t("origin.title")}
	heroImage="../../images/web/FATHER_dark.jpg"
	description=""
>
	<Trans i18nKey="origin.part1">
		<center><h1>PART I: One-Man Show</h1></center>
		<p>
			Our society was born from an entity in constant pain, a human
			being like you or me, with a life so miserable that it is
			'forgettable'; he fled for a long time in his own mind, thinking
			and dreaming of new worlds and alternate histories to those of
			our world. Eventually he made the decision to archive and share
			these worlds that gave him so much fear and comfort over the
			years. That's how <strong>ANALOGIUM</strong> was born... yet is not
			the end of our story.
		</p>
		<p>
			Although the project filled our founding father with life, the
			work was too much and soon, along with private events, took its
			toll on his mental state. He knew he needed help, but all the
			time he spent locked in his own dome ended his ability to go out
			and talk to other humans. He became a hermit, and finding
			someone as fallen and broken as he was was practically
			impossible... until <i>she</i> arrived to his life.
		</p>
	</Trans>
	<Trans i18nKey="origin.part2">
		<center><h1>PART II: From Bliss to Feeling Half-Death</h1></center>
		<p>
			'<i>Lady</i>' was everything to our creator, she was the only
			person in a long time to understand and heal the creator's
			mental wounds. He himself described her as '<i>a fallen angel</i>
			'... But unfortunately nothing good can last for anyone, and one
			day 'Lady' evaporated from our father's life. This left him completely
			devastated, he didn't smile, he didn't see, he didn't move, he was
			just present, lifeless.
		</p>
		<p>
			Nobody knows for sure what broke our founder's fairytale, not
			even the ones closest to him; the only thing he allows himself
			to say is: <b><i><a href={localizePath("/fault")} id="hid">It Was My Fault
			</a></i></b>
		</p>
	</Trans>
	<Trans i18nKey="origin.part3">
		<center><h1>PART III: Among Ashes</h1></center>
		<p>
			It took a long time for our founder to heal, full of empty
			replacements, insane acts and feelings amplified by his own
			pain; until in a monument of clarity, the stories that had
			locked him in his mind for so long resounded in his mind, and he
			found something that made him happy again, however temporary it
			seemed. He worked as hardly as he could but at last, he felt
			whole. Now our founding father was not alone, he managed to find
			a team that had the same mind as him. <b><i>He Found a Family</i>
			</b>
		</p>
	</Trans>
</Layout>
